    {
      "finding": "The two captures of the same URL, ~1 hour apart, share 22 players with zero disagreements on practice or game status, while capture B carries 46 rows capture A never rendered (four of them 'Out'). The page renders club tables progressively, so a single pass silently under-reports.",
      "action": "Ingestion must fetch until the per-club row count is stable across two consecutive renders, record (timestamp, row count, chunk coverage) with every capture, and reconcile before anything downstream consumes 'who is Out'. A truncated render looks exactly like a quiet week."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Blank Game Status is the majority case even on a full render: 37 of 68 rows here have a blank Injuries cell and many rows carry a practice status with no designation. Absence of a designation is the report's way of saying 'certain to play' only for players who practised fully, and it is indistinguishable from 'not updated yet' on a truncated render.",
      "action": "Store blank as NULL with a reason flag ('undisclosed', 'not-in-this-render'); never impute availability, and never let the model treat a truncation artefact as a health signal."
    },
